# cp.async with a register src-size, 16 on lanes 0..15 and 0 on the
# others: ptxas writes LDGSTS with an ignore-src predicate. The register
# is not read, so which lanes read, and how much, is not known: the row,
# the per-execution read and the totals are bounds, within which Nsight
# Compute's 8 sectors over the launch fall.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: global load <= 16 B (predicated)  warp: <= 17 sectors (ideal <= 16)
CHECK: per thread per execution: global load <= 16 B; shared store 16 B
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load <= 1024 B, store 0 B
CHECK: AI(global) >= 0 flop/B
CHECK: measured L2 sectors of global accesses: 1 lines agree (0 exact, 0 within a range, 1 within a bound), 0 differ
